// layer L1
// Output fixed by DESIGN.md (at 843be85) line 1813: "A `rat` is kept reduced with a positive
// denominator and printed `1r/3r`; `/` by `0r` is `#divByZero`"; line 1817: `rat(s)` reads what
// `Utf8String` writes (`3r`, `-1r/3r`) or the same without the `r`s. `f64` of a `rat` is the
// nearest float, ties to even (DESIGN sec:corner_cases "Casts are domain proofs", step L1.18,
// author P355), so `f64(third)` is 0.3333333333333333 and its `else` is never taken.
main(m: MainArgs) {
  d = rat(trim(m.stdin[0] else "")) else 1r;
  third = 1r / 3r;
  m.stdout <- "${third + 1r / 6r} ${0.1r + 0.2r} ${third * 3r} ${f64(third) else -1.0} ${(1r / d) else 0r}";
}
